```sh\n# 1. Build the XS oracle submodule (needed for the differential targets — see above).\n# 2. Install the pinned nightly + cargo-fuzz (the pin lives in\n#    rust/engine/ironhorse-fuzz/fuzz/rust-toolchain.toml, no longer only in CI):\nrustup toolchain install nightly-2026-08-15 --profile minimal\ncargo install cargo-fuzz --locked\n# 3. Run any target from the fuzz project (the toolchain file selects the nightly):\ncd rust/engine/ironhorse-fuzz\ncargo fuzz run parser            # or differential_compile, snapshot_decoder, bytecode_decoder, …\ncargo fuzz run parser -- -max_total_time=30   # bounded, mirrors the old CI smoke\n```\n\nThe maintained targets are `differential_source`, `bytecode_decoder`,\n`differential_stage2b`, `differential_regexp`, `differential_regexp_surface`,\n`parser`, `differential_compile`, `snapshot_roundtrip`, and `snapshot_decoder`.\nCrashing inputs land in `fuzz/artifacts/`; reduce with `cargo fuzz tmin <target>\n<input>`. A finding's durable regression is a Rust unit test in `ironhorse-vm` (the\n`fuzz/corpus` and `fuzz/artifacts` trees are gitignored, so a corpus seed cannot be\na committed regression).\n\n## Running the harness\n\n```sh\ncd rust/engine\ncargo run -p ironhorse-262 --bin harness          # stage-1 corpus\ncargo run -p ironhorse-262 --bin harness -- '1 + 2 * 3'   # ad-hoc program\ncargo test  --workspace -- --test-threads=1   # includes the bar as a test\n\n# The xst-analogue test262 runner (`endot-ih`, design § Part 2) — the\n# dual-run runner that subsumes the retired `test262-language` walker.\n# Run per subtree — the XS oracle accumulates memory across a whole-tree\n# walk, so `expressions`/`statements` in separate processes bound the RSS.\ncargo run -p ironhorse-262 --bin endot-ih -- expressions\ncargo run -p ironhorse-262 --bin endot-ih -- statements/for\n# The stage-3 built-ins sections run through the same binary:\ncargo run -p ironhorse-262 --bin endot-ih -- built-ins/Boolean\n# Pinned nightly for the ironhorse-fuzz cargo-fuzz targets.\n#\n# Fuzzing has moved OUT of pull-request CI (the `fuzz-ironhorse` job was removed) and\n# is driven continuously in the background by a garden service instead. This pin used\n# to live ONLY in that CI job's `FUZZ_TOOLCHAIN` env; it is relocated here so local\n# runs stay reproducible and share one source of truth. With this file present,\n# `cargo fuzz run <target>` from this `fuzz/` directory uses the pinned nightly\n# automatically (no `+nightly-…` needed). Bump deliberately, validated against the\n# whole target set.\n[toolchain]\nchannel = \"nightly-2026-08-15\"\nprofile = \"minimal\"\n# cargo-fuzz manifest for the ironhorse-fuzz targets (design § Fuzzability).\n# Run locally with `cargo fuzz run <target>` from this directory (the sibling\n# rust-toolchain.toml pins the nightly, so no `+nightly-…` is needed); not part of\n# the engine workspace build (kept out via the parent's default-members). The\n# comparison and generation logic lives in the ironhorse-fuzz lib, which the\n# engine workspace builds and unit-tests without a libFuzzer toolchain.\n#\n# NOTE: fuzzing no longer runs in pull-request CI — a garden background service\n# drives these targets continuously over a persistent corpus and files each finding\n# as a standing repair PR. These targets remain fully runnable locally.\n[package]\nname = \"ironhorse-fuzz-targets\"\nversion = \"0.0.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\npublish = false\n\n[package.metadata]\ncargo-fuzz = true\n\n[dependencies]\nlibfuzzer-sys = \"0.4\"\nironhorse-fuzz = { path = \"..\" }\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"differential_source\"\npath = \"fuzz_targets/differential_source.rs\"\ntest = false\ndoc = false\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"bytecode_decoder\"\npath = \"fuzz_targets/bytecode_decoder.rs\"\ntest = false\ndoc = false\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"differential_stage2b\"\npath = \"fuzz_targets/differential_stage2b.rs\"\ntest = false\ndoc = false\n\n[[bin]]\nname = \"differential_regexp\"\npath = \"fuzz_targets/differential_regexp.rs\"